    "note": "Team 445 describes both CTPA and V/Q as options when imaging is needed. The Gift key is preserved; the stem does not supply enough context to make one scan universally preferred.",
    "explanation": "First assess the probability of pulmonary embolism using a pregnancy-adapted pathway. Ultrasound can help when there are symptoms of DVT. If chest imaging is needed, both CTPA and V/Q are options. Chest X-ray findings, contrast suitability and the local pathway help choose the test."
